  "headingText": "Sec. 31-4.5. Obstructing identification.",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "citation",
      "text": "(720 ILCS 5/31-4.5)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Sec. 31-4.5. Obstructing identification."
    },
    {
      "type": "subsection",
      "label": "(a)",
      "text": "(a) A person commits the offense of obstructing identification when he or she intentionally or knowingly furnishes a false or fictitious name, residence address, or date of birth to a peace officer who has:"
    },
    {
      "type": "subsection",
      "label": "(1)",
      "text": "(1) lawfully arrested the person;"
    },
    {
      "type": "subsection",
      "label": "(2)",
      "text": "(2) lawfully detained the person; or"
    },
    {
      "type": "subsection",
      "label": "(3)",
      "text": "(3) requested the information from a person that the peace officer has good cause to believe is a witness to a criminal offense. (b) Sentence. Obstructing identification is a Class A misdemeanor."
    },
    {
      "type": "source",
      "text": "(Source: P.A. 96-335, eff. 1-1-10.)"
    }
  ],
